{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.BarReflectionGridSelection","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.BarReflectionGridSelection","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Group.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Set.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Group","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Group.Int.Even"],"declarations":9,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.BarReflectionGridSelection.grid_barInvariant_classification","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.BarReflectionGridSelection.grid_barInvariant_classification","kind":"theorem","line":124,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/BarReflectionGridSelection.lean#L124-L192","doc":"**The two-point classification.** Suppose the step has a half-step\n`w` (`w² = v`) and `G` is 2-torsion-free (both hold in `ℝ_{>0}`). Then\na grid class is bar-invariant iff it is the unit class `grid 1 v` or\nthe half-step class `grid w v` — the two named candidates of the\nextension-circle question, separated by exactly half a `q̃`-step\n(the KSel-1 discriminant). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.BarReflectionGridSelection.grid_barInvariant_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.BarReflectionGridSelection.grid_barInvariant_iff","kind":"theorem","line":110,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/BarReflectionGridSelection.lean#L110-L122","doc":"**Bar-invariance criterion.** The grid class of `u` is fixed by the\nbar reflection iff `u² ∈ v^ℤ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.BarReflectionGridSelection.grid_eq_grid_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.BarReflectionGridSelection.grid_eq_grid_iff","kind":"theorem","line":94,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/BarReflectionGridSelection.lean#L94-L108","doc":"Grid equality is translate equivalence: `grid u v = grid w v` iff\n`w = u · v^k` for some `k : ℤ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.BarReflectionGridSelection.barReflect_mem_grid_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.BarReflectionGridSelection.barReflect_mem_grid_iff","kind":"theorem","line":84,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/BarReflectionGridSelection.lean#L84-L92","doc":"The bar reflection acts on translate classes by `u ↦ u⁻¹`:\nmembership form, both directions. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.BarReflectionGridSelection.barReflect_mem_grid","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.BarReflectionGridSelection.barReflect_mem_grid","kind":"theorem","line":73,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/BarReflectionGridSelection.lean#L73-L82","doc":"The bar reflection maps the grid through `u` into the grid through\n`u⁻¹`: `barReflect v (u · v^k) = u⁻¹ · v^(−k−1)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.BarReflectionGridSelection.barReflect_involutive","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.BarReflectionGridSelection.barReflect_involutive","kind":"theorem","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/BarReflectionGridSelection.lean#L67-L71","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.BarReflectionGridSelection.barReflect","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.BarReflectionGridSelection.barReflect","kind":"def","line":63,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/BarReflectionGridSelection.lean#L63-L65","doc":"The **bar reflection** `s ↦ v⁻¹ · s⁻¹` (archimedean reading:\n`s ↦ q̃⁻¹/s`, the fibre bar involution on the Schwinger variable). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.BarReflectionGridSelection.mem_grid_self","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.BarReflectionGridSelection.mem_grid_self","kind":"theorem","line":60,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/BarReflectionGridSelection.lean#L60-L61","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.BarReflectionGridSelection.grid","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.BarReflectionGridSelection.grid","kind":"def","line":54,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/BarReflectionGridSelection.lean#L54-L58","doc":"The **theta grid** through `u` with multiplicative step `v`\n(archimedean reading: `v = q̃ = √q`, the balanced half-step; the grid is\nthe support `u · q̃^ℤ` of an atomic representing kernel). ","signatureChunk":0}]}